{
  "contract_version": 1,
  "change_id": "M453-pr-run-queue-hygiene-superseded-only-20261105",
  "human_scope_review": "Owner explicitly requested on 2026-11-04 automatic cancellation of superseded PR workflow runs, keeping only latest commit checks, preserving unrelated PRs/main builds, and avoiding broad reruns. This scope changes only top-level workflow event/concurrency headers plus two new narrowly scoped workflows and a regression test. M453 cancellation is limited to authenticated same-repository open PRs and older head SHAs; main/push/manual/fork runs are protected. Existing required finance tests and workflow path filters remain intact. Human review and exact-head CI remain mandatory.",
  "user_requested_changes": [
    "Prevent duplicate queued/running PR runs for an older commit by adding workflow-specific PR-number concurrency groups and PR-only cancel-in-progress to PR workflows currently missing this protection.",
    "Keep main push/Android APK builds, other PRs and manual workflow_dispatch runs independent by using the run_id fallback and event-limited cancellation.",
    "Provide a trusted default-branch PR supersession cleaner that cancels only old still-active pull_request runs on the same open same-repository main-targeting PR; exclude forks, main, current SHA, other PRs and completed jobs.",
    "Offer a manual GitHub Actions dispatch with dry-run enabled by default, plus a limited after-merge sweep of recently updated PRs, without accessing user financial data.",
    "Retain existing path-based workflow triggers and required financial SQLCipher/CI checks; avoid full re-run after an isolated failure, prefer selective GitHub failed-job retry.",
    "Add exact-head safe-concurrency regression tests, bounded change-scope documentation and release notes."
  ],
